course: dictionary
lesson: 4960
title: Careless words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you how someone does something. «The boy incautiously leaned over the edge» tells you how he leaned: without care. The words around it are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: Look at the picture the words paint. Leaning over an edge is dangerous, so someone who does it incautiously is not thinking about the danger. Try your meaning in the sentence: "carelessly" fits, so incautiously means carelessly.
explain: Now read «The Rat incautiously tells Toad that the Mole and the Badger will be out till luncheon time.» The Rat speaks without thinking first, and the result is that Toad knows he will be alone with the Rat. The word shows that careless talk can have consequences.
fact: Incautiously is an adverb: it tells you how someone does an action.
fact: Incautiously means without care, carelessly, without thinking about danger or consequences.
fact: Caution means care, and cautious means careful; the in- at the start shows the opposite, so incautious means not careful.
fact: «Spoke incautiously» means said things without thinking first.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice incautiously mentions her cat Dinah to the Mouse and the birds, and they all run away.
exercise: «The boy incautiously leaned over the edge of the bridge.» What does incautiously mean? | Quietly, so nobody could hear | Happily, with a big smile | Very slowly and with great care | *Carelessly, without thinking about danger
exercise: Alice incautiously mentions her cat Dinah to the Mouse and the birds. What happens next? | *They all run away | They invite her to tea | They ask her to sing a song | They all clap and cheer
exercise: Which word means carelessly in «He spoke incautiously and got into trouble»? | got | spoke | trouble | *incautiously
test: «She incautiously left the gate open, and the sheep ran out.» What does incautiously mean here? | Slowly and quietly | Carefully, with great thought | Happily and proudly | *Carelessly, without thinking
test: Which sentence shows someone acting incautiously? | She checked the ice before she stepped on it | He read the sign and then waited for the bus | *He leaned far over the edge of the cliff without a thought | They tied the rope tightly and climbed slowly
exam: «The Rat incautiously tells Toad that the Mole and the Badger will be out till luncheon time.» Why does Toad now know he will be alone with the Rat? | *Because the Rat's careless words told Toad that the Mole and the Badger would be away | Because Toad read a letter from the Badger | Because the Mole and the Badger asked Toad to stay | Because the Rat thought carefully before speaking
